<section id="bbs016" image-layout="blank"><card-template-instructions>A two-series line chart beside a takeaway rail: the plot takes the wide column, the rail carries a label, a short statement and one supporting sentence; values are plain numbers.</card-template-instructions><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item colspan="37" vertical-align="center" id="1sbCCQ5TmL"><graph height="300pt" width="520pt" text-size="md" y-axis-min="0" chart-type="line"><properties><property type="label" label="Week" key="week"></property><property type="data" label="Plan" key="plan"></property><property type="data" label="Actual" key="actual"></property></properties><data><row><cell>Wk 1</cell><cell>310</cell><cell>296</cell></row><row><cell>Wk 2</cell><cell>315</cell><cell>318</cell></row><row><cell>Wk 3</cell><cell>320</cell><cell>341</cell></row><row><cell>Wk 4</cell><cell>325</cell><cell>352</cell></row><row><cell>Wk 5</cell><cell>330</cell><cell>349</cell></row><row><cell>Wk 6</cell><cell>335</cell><cell>371</cell></row></data></graph><p font-size="sm">Weekly orders, plan versus actual, second quarter.</p></grid-item><grid-item colspan="23" vertical-align="center" id="TW_iZvjUt8"><labels><label variant="solid">Week 3</label></labels><h3>The second delivery day started here</h3><p>Actual orders crossed the plan the week regional accounts moved to two deliveries and stayed above it for the rest of the quarter.</p></grid-item></grid></section>